lamco-rdp-server (1.4.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 1.4.5
  * Cross-build aware debian/rules (arm64 via dpkg-buildpackage -a arm64)
  * Area capture on GNOME so a fullscreen video no longer freezes the session
    (capture.gnome_record_mode)
  * VA-API hardware encoding now drives EGFX H.264 (AVC444 and AVC420);
    desktop audio capture now actually starts and stays in sync
  * Server-driven cursor shapes, multitouch over MS-RDPEI, the client's
    keyboard layout applied, RTT and bandwidth reported to the client
  * Fix server crash on client disconnect (lamco-pipewire no longer calls
    pw_deinit); fix configured listen port resetting to 3389
  * Fix a GNOME server that could stop accepting connections after a client
    connect (EIS handshake lost its wakeup); fix the first connection after
    an audio-enabled client disconnects failing on a stale RDPSND wave
  * Hyper-V Enhanced Session Mode via security_mode = "rdp"; libei video
    persistence on KDE; EIS input reliability and reconnect-storm fix
  * Rename systemd user unit to app-io.lamco.rdp-server.service (Alias kept;
    postinst migrates enabled state for logged-in users)
  * New Depends: fuse3; new Recommends: vainfo; postinst enables
    user_allow_other in /etc/fuse.conf
  * MSRV 1.94; libpipewire >= 0.3.62 required by lamco-pipewire 0.6

 -- Greg Lamberson <greg@lamco.io>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500

lamco-rdp-server (1.4.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 1.4.4
  * Unified multi-transport accept layer: AF_VSOCK for Hyper-V Enhanced Session
    Mode, plus experimental WebSocket and RDCleanPath
  * Vulkan Video H.264 encoder and an HTTP metrics and health server
  * Per-connection session lifecycle on GNOME, so the server handles many
    sequential sessions without a restart
  * KDE, sway, and COSMIC capture and clipboard fixes; Linux-to-Windows file
    copy on native installs; many GUI fixes
  * systemd unit hardening fix so PAM authentication works under the unit
  * MSRV 1.89, Rust edition 2024
  * License revision: Licensor Lamco Development LLC, Change Date 2029-06-01

 -- Greg Lamberson <greg@lamco.io>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0500

lamco-rdp-server (1.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release
  * Fix Unicode keyboard mapping: map Unicode events to evdev keycodes
  * PipeWire stream DRIVER flag: ensure frames at negotiated framerate
  * Fix Wayland WouldBlock handling in event loop
  * Fix MIME charset handling for clipboard text negotiation
  * Upgrade pipewire-rs to 0.9.2 via lamco-pipewire 0.3.1
  * Fix PipeWire format negotiation for audio capture

 -- Greg Lamberson <greg@lamco.io>  Mon, 10 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000

lamco-rdp-server (1.4.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix systemd service: move StartLimitIntervalSec/Burst to [Unit] section
  * Fix systemd service: allow mount/umount2 syscalls for FUSE clipboard
  * Fix systemd service: remove capability directives that crash in
    unprivileged environments (Ubuntu 24.04 in Proxmox)
  * Fix systemd service: remove ProtectHome=read-only (hangs KDE plasmashell)
  * Add libfuse3-3 | libfuse3-4 alternative dependency for Ubuntu/Debian compat

